  "notes": "PROMPT_GT_MISMATCH: prompt says to export the VPC CIDR, both AZ names and the security group ID, but the ground truth gives Export names only to the VPC ID and four subnet IDs (the other four outputs have no Export). So all nine values are checked only as outputs; Export is required for at least five. The prompt's 'each private subnet routes through its own AZ NAT gateway' is checked as two private NAT routes in distinct route tables with distinct NAT gateways; AZ pairing is not expressible. Endpoint SG ingress is not checked. Retention and traffic type must actually be wired to a parameter (the log group / flow log value equals a parameter default, or a parameter with no default). An SG with no egress rules keeps CloudFormation's default allow-all egress, so sg_no_open_egress requires egress rules to exist. Not expressible: that NAT gateways sit in the public subnets and the ECR endpoints in the private ones (no way to classify a subnet), and that the S3 endpoint is on every route table (len_gte 3 = one public + two private). Scored on 5 real candidates: GLM53F's flow-log role trusts delivery.logs.amazonaws.com (VPC flow logs assume vpc-flow-logs.amazonaws.com) and DSV4F's endpoint SG has no egress rules (default allow-all); both contradict the prompt and the checks stay."
